From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niko Lowry <niko@neeks.me>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:49:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] llm: size the predicted KV cache per layer

PredictServerVRAM sized every layer's KV cache with the smallest
head_count_kv, embedding_length/head_count as the head size, the full
context, and f16. For models that differ per layer that is far off.
gemma4:31b at 262144 context with OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 was
predicted at 57.9 GiB; llama-server allocated 31.0 GiB. The scheduler
evicted models to make room the load never needed, and the inflated
prediction also triggered metal_partial_offload, which turns off mmap.

The estimate now follows llama.cpp's allocation: per-layer
head_count_kv, key_length and value_length (with the _swa variants),
sliding-window layers holding window plus one batch per sequence,
no cache for layers without KV heads or for non-causal models, and
the configured cache type. Unquantized caches size V at the widest
layer, as llama.cpp does without flash attention.

Predictions on an M5 Max against llama-server's own allocation
(weights + KV + compute), q8_0 cache:

  gemma4:31b        262144   57.9 -> 30.4 GiB   measured 31.0
  qwen3-coder-next  262144   54.2 -> 51.4 GiB   measured 52.4
  phi4-mini         131072   18.3 -> 10.8 GiB   measured 12.0

The gemma4 KV estimate matches llama-server to the MiB at -ub 2048
(12155 MiB). The compute graph is still not counted, as before; the
scheduler's 20% headroom covers it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
